+# Residual-room selection
+
+`room_policy=all_rooms` returns the exact selected canonical source.
+`room_policy=largest_room` first executes that program, then recolors the unique
+largest four-connected cyan component to green (3). Original gray-area ranking
+is not equivalent: three-cell arm runs consume cells inside rooms. Red arms and
+unselected cyan rooms remain unchanged. Racket ties (outside the sampled unique
+maximum grammar) select the row-major first component; an empty candidate set
+leaves the canonical output unchanged.
+
+The adapter uses the approved builder's room/bridge/one-cell-tip/three-cell-arm/
+T-cap grammar directly, not its official bitmap replay branch. Ordinary scenes
+are one connected gray network. The separate 30x30 extension has four separated
+seven-room networks, one per quadrant, with genuine arm interactions and one
+unique six-cell residual room; its quadrant is shuffled. Networks are anchored
+to opposite boundaries, not merely centered on a larger blank canvas. This
+extension does not change production generation, limits, or safety decisions.
+
+Two constructive demonstrations reject the declared finite rivals; requesting
+more demonstrations adds independent scenes, up to six. Every seed constructs
+six demos and four distinct queries using independent RNG streams. Requests
+return prefixes, so demo/query counts and settings cannot influence earlier
+inputs. Four queries are controller-private. Call `public_turn(episode,index)`
+for a fresh value containing only demonstrations and that query's input; it
+contains no settings, programs, answers, future inputs or total-count hint.
+Do not send the controller's full four-query example file as a first user turn.
+
+## Re-run the bounded evidence
+From the packet's outer folder:
+
+```sh
+python3 review.py run python3 generators/c1b540a1d7b0/workspace/parametric/audit.py --seeds 20 --out ../checks/c1b540a1d7b0/audit-new
+python3 review.py task-tests c1b540a1d7b0 --phase after --out ../checks/c1b540a1d7b0/tests-new
+```
+
+Choose new output directories; the audit refuses overwrites. `audit.py` is a
+portable task-local harness that dynamically reads this adapter's contract.
+It sweeps independent counts, tests input matching and prefix identity, mutates
+private/future fields to check projection independence, writes public-byte-hashed
+challenges and individual turns, and compares native programs and executable
+rivals with protected Racket. Python sweep claims and protected labels are
+reported separately. No owner acceptance or training admission is performed.
+
+`evidence/current/report.json` retains the failed original stress sweep: seed 7
+exhausted the joint coverage/unique-winner sampler. The fix constructs coverage
+and the winner separately. `evidence/current-v2/` is the passing replacement.
+The first two demonstrations are checked against canonical, first, last,
+smallest, all-cyan and largest-pre-arm-thick-region rules. This finite set does
+not prove universal identifiability. The existing production bitmap-replay audit
+is not resolved or silently upgraded by this parametric-only repair.
